<h1>Stylist Services Agreement</h1>
<p class="meta"><strong>Last updated:</strong> <span class="tbd">[DATE]</span> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>Effective date:</strong> <span class="tbd">[DATE]</span></p>

<p>This Stylist Services Agreement (the "<strong>Stylist Agreement</strong>") is a supplement to the armoires <a href="https://armoires.io/terms">Terms of Service</a> (the "<strong>Terms</strong>") and <a href="https://armoires.io/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. It applies to you only if you choose to operate as a <strong>Stylist</strong> on armoires. Capitalized terms not defined here have the meaning given in the Terms.</p>

<p>By setting up a studio, enabling stylist features, or providing Styling Services, you agree to this Stylist Agreement. If you do not agree, do not operate as a Stylist. <strong>This Agreement does not change your rights as a personal (client) user.</strong></p>

<h3>Definitions</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Stylist</strong> — a user who offers styling services to other users through the Service.</li>
  <li><strong>Client</strong> — a user who requests or receives styling services from a Stylist.</li>
  <li><strong>Styling Services</strong> — reviewing a Client's shared wardrobe and preferences, assembling and proposing looks, delivering a recommended look, and related communication, all performed through the Service.</li>
  <li><strong>Client Content</strong> — the wardrobe items, photos, closet, briefs, inspiration references, measurements or fit notes, messages, and other information a Client shares with you through the Service.</li>
</ul>

<h2>1. Eligibility to Be a Stylist</h2>
<p>You must be at least <strong>18 years old</strong> and able to form a binding contract. You represent that all information in your studio profile (name, tagline, specialties, rates, experience) is <strong>accurate and not misleading</strong>, and that you will keep it current.</p>
<div class="reviewnote"><span class="tag">Review note</span> Consider whether any identity or business verification is required before a Stylist can be discoverable or receive payment.</div>

<h2>2. Independent Contractor — No Employment or Agency</h2>
<p>You are an <strong>independent contractor</strong>. Nothing in this Agreement creates an employment, agency, partnership, joint venture, or franchise relationship between you and armoires. You are not authorized to act for, bind, or make commitments on behalf of armoires, and you may not represent otherwise. You are solely responsible for how you provide Styling Services, for your own equipment and expenses, and for all <strong>taxes</strong> on amounts you earn.</p>
<div class="reviewnote"><span class="tag">Review note</span> At payment launch, add 1099 issuance and tax-information (W-9/W-8) requirements — see Section 7.</div>

<h2>3. The Stylist–Client Relationship; armoires Is a Venue</h2>
<p>armoires provides a <strong>platform</strong> that lets Stylists and Clients find one another and work together. <strong>The styling relationship is solely between you and your Client.</strong> armoires is <strong>not a party</strong> to it, does not provide Styling Services, does not supervise or control how you style, and does not guarantee you any clients, engagements, or earnings. You are responsible for the quality, timeliness, and lawfulness of your Styling Services.</p>

<h2>4. Client Closet Access and Data — Your Core Obligations</h2>
<p>Access to a Client's wardrobe is a <strong>privilege granted by the Client</strong> through the Service's consent mechanism (an active styling engagement), and it can be <strong>revoked at any time</strong>. You agree that:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>(a) Purpose limitation.</strong> You will access and use Client Content <strong>only</strong> to provide Styling Services to that Client, and for no other purpose.</li>
  <li><strong>(b) No copying or redistribution.</strong> You will not download, screenshot, copy, scrape, sell, publish, or share Client Content outside the Service, and you will not use it to train any model or build any dataset.</li>
  <li><strong>(c) No retention after access ends.</strong> When an engagement ends or the Client revokes access, you will stop accessing and using that Client's Content and delete any copies within your control.</li>
  <li><strong>(d) Confidentiality.</strong> You will treat Client Content as confidential and protect it from unauthorized disclosure.</li>
  <li><strong>(e) Privacy compliance.</strong> You will comply with the Privacy Policy and applicable data-protection laws in your handling of Client Content.</li>
  <li><strong>(f) No harvesting.</strong> You will not solicit a Client's contact details or personal data to move the relationship off-platform, and you will not use closet access to identify, locate, or contact a Client outside the Service.</li>
</ul>
<p>Breach of this Section is grounds for immediate suspension or termination of your stylist status and may result in liability to armoires and the Client.</p>

<h2>5. Your Portfolio and Content</h2>
<p>Your studio profile, uploaded looks, notes, and portfolio are <strong>Your Content</strong> under the Terms, and the license and responsibilities there apply. You represent that you have all rights necessary to post any inspiration images, references, brand names, or third-party materials you use, and that they do not infringe anyone's intellectual-property, privacy, or publicity rights. You will not misrepresent your credentials, experience, affiliations, or results.</p>

<h2>6. Reviews and Ratings</h2>
<p>Clients may rate and review you after a delivery, and armoires may display those reviews on your profile and in the directory. You will <strong>not</strong> offer incentives for positive reviews, post fake reviews, or manipulate ratings. armoires may remove reviews that violate the Terms but is not obligated to monitor them.</p>

<h2>7. Fees, Payments, and Payouts <span class="notyet">Effective at payment launch</span></h2>
<p><em>This Section is <strong>effective only when paid stylist features launch</strong>. Until then, Styling Services are provided without payment through the Service, and any arrangement to exchange value is solely between you and your Client and outside armoires' responsibility.</em></p>
<p>When paid features launch:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Client charges.</strong> You set your rates within the options the Service provides. Clients are charged through our third-party payment processor (<strong>Stripe</strong>, including Stripe Connect).</li>
  <li><strong>Service fee / commission.</strong> armoires may retain a <span class="tbd">[commission of X% / a fee of $Y]</span> of each transaction as a platform fee, disclosed before you are charged or paid.</li>
  <li><strong>Payouts.</strong> Amounts owed to you (net of fees and adjustments) are paid to your connected Stripe account on <span class="tbd">[Stripe's standard payout schedule / a schedule we disclose]</span>. <strong>You must complete Stripe tax onboarding — providing a valid Form W-9 (U.S. persons) or Form W-8 (non-U.S. persons), plus identity and bank information — before you can receive payouts.</strong> armoires does not store your bank, card, or full tax-identification details; Stripe does, under <span class="tbd">[Stripe's Connected Account Agreement]</span>, which you also agree to.</li>
  <li><strong>Refunds, disputes, and chargebacks.</strong> <span class="tbd">[Refund/cancellation policy, who bears chargebacks, and how service-quality disputes are handled — to be defined.]</span></li>
  <li><strong>Taxes — your responsibility to file; our responsibility to report.</strong> You are solely responsible for reporting and paying all taxes on your earnings (including income and self-employment taxes). Separately, because payments are facilitated through the Service, <strong>we or Stripe will issue you an IRS Form 1099-K</strong> (and file the corresponding information return) if your activity meets the applicable federal or state reporting thresholds for a tax year.</li>
  <li><strong>No off-platform circumvention.</strong> You will not arrange payment for Service-originated engagements outside the Service to avoid fees.</li>
</ul>
<div class="reviewnote"><span class="tag">Review note</span> Commission structure (flat %, tiered, or subscription), refund/chargeback policy, and 1099-K thresholds (federal + state, which change year to year) are open business/CPA decisions. Stripe Connect can generate and file the 1099-K on the platform's behalf. Sales-tax treatment of the styling service is a separate analysis.</div>

<h2>8. Prohibited Conduct (Stylists)</h2>
<p>In addition to the Terms' Acceptable Use rules, you will not: (a) misuse Client closet access as described in Section 4; (b) provide advice you present as licensed professional advice (medical, financial, legal) — Styling Services are personal opinion and taste; (c) discriminate against or harass Clients; (d) make false claims about products, availability, pricing, or outcomes; or (e) circumvent platform fees.</p>

<h2>9. Suspension and Termination of Stylist Status</h2>
<p>You may stop being a Stylist at any time by <span class="tbd">[disabling your studio / contacting support]</span>. armoires may suspend or terminate your stylist status (while leaving your personal account intact, at our discretion) for breach of this Agreement or the Terms, or to protect users or the Service. On termination: your access to Client closets ends immediately; obligations that by their nature survive (Sections 2, 4, 5, 7 payments owed, 10, and 11) continue; and pending payouts are handled per Section 7 and applicable law.</p>

